@title A letter from Corbel & Finch
@subtitle About our Elm Street store

Dear friends,

## What is changing
For 17 years our Elm Street shop has been a place to find a book and talk about it with someone who cares. After we trade on 2026-12-23, the Elm Street shop closes for good.

Our Harbor Road shop, our online shop and our school book fairs all carry on.

## Why
When the Elm Street lease renews on 2027-01-01, the rent will rise by 70 percent. More than half of our sales now happen at Harbor Road or online. We chose to keep the two places that are growing.

We know this is hard news, and we did not make the decision lightly.

## What stays the same
Gift certificates and store credit are honored at Harbor Road and online until 2027-12-31. Your loyalty points move over automatically, so there is nothing for you to do.

The six booksellers from Elm Street are moving to Harbor Road. You will see the same faces, and the same care for what you read.

## How to say goodbye
Please come and say goodbye. Our last Saturday story hour is on 2026-12-19 at 11:00. A farewell evening with our staff and local authors is on 2026-12-22, from 17:00 to 20:00.

All stock at Elm Street is 20 percent off from 2026-11-28.

Thank you for every visit, every recommendation and every book you have brought home. It has meant a great deal to us.

Marguerite Pell, owner
